{
  "name": "What to Expect During Your Drywall Remodeling Project",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Embarking on a drywall remodeling project can transform a room, but knowing what’s involved helps set expectations. Generally, the process kicks off with precise measurements and cutting drywall boards to fit your space, whether it's a full room or just a section. Then, those boards are securely fastened to the framing. This is followed by taping the seams, which creates a smooth surface for the joint compound. You'll see several applications of joint compound, each requiring sanding once dry. This drying time is crucial; it often needs a full day between coats, and rushing it can lead to issues down the line. After all the sanding and smoothing, the walls are ready for priming and painting. For areas like bathrooms or kitchens, we’ll make sure to use the correct type of moisture-resistant drywall, addressing any potential moisture issues beforehand. The timeline can vary; a single room might be 1-2 days of installation, but the finishing work, drying, and texturing can easily extend the project. It’s a process that requires patience and precision to achieve that flawless finish you’re looking for. We at HH Remodeling LLC are here to guide you through every step in Aurora and the greater Denver area.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
